  "Correct Block-vs-Reliability framing: cite zenoh's own docs showing CongestionControl and Reliability are orthogonal knobs; reposition the claim as 'Block's local-only semantics are not surfaced to users' rather than 'Block fails its end-to-end contract.'",
  "Run the evaluation_prosecutor's killer experiment: 4-node topology (1 pub → 1 router → [1 slow sub + 1 fast sub]). If the router maintains throughput to the fast sub while dropping for the slow sub, per-hop isolation is a deliberate feature, not a defect. This experiment disambiguates 'failure' from 'design.'",
  "Statistical rigor: ≥3 independent trials per condition with CIs; explain the 41-64% variance across runs; sweep N in the 3-node test to characterize buffer-fill threshold; decompose per-hop loss (pub→router vs router→sub) with counters, not inference.",
